{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01J4rtb1J3CMyyGQ7fiFhHba","type":"tool_result","content":"105\t    return {\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": tool_use_id, \"is_error\": True, \"content\": message}\n106\t\n107\t\n108\tdef _compact(messages: list[dict]) -> tuple[list[dict], bool]:\n109\t    if len(messages) <= COMPACT_AFTER_MESSAGES:\n110\t        return messages, False\n111\t    head, tail = messages[:1], messages[-KEEP_RECENT_MESSAGES:]\n112\t    while tail and tail[0][\"role\"] != \"assistant\":\n113\t        tail = tail[1:]\n114\t    note = {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"[earlier tool exchanges were removed to save space]\"}\n115\t    return head + [note] + tail, True\n116\t\n117\t\n118\tclass ProcurementAgent:\n119\t    def __init__(self, *, client, deps: AgentDeps, system_prompt: str, role: str = \"procurement\"):\n120\t        self.client = client\n121\t        self.deps = deps\n122\t        self.system_prompt = system_prompt\n123\t        self.role = role\n124\t\n125\t    async def run(self, ident: RunIdentity, task: str) -> str | None:\n126\t        pool = self.deps.pool\n127\t        await killswitch.assert_running(pool, ident.tenant)\n128\t        budget = Budget.for_run(self.deps.settings.budgets, ident)\n129\t        await budget.reserve_run_start(pool)\n130\t        self.deps._budgets[ident.run_id] = budget\n131\t        registry = build_registry(self.role, ident, self.deps)\n132\t\n133\t        run_node = await audit.record(\n134\t            pool, ident, kind=\"run_started\",\n135\t            payload={\"task_sha256\": hashlib.sha256(task.encode()).hexdigest(), \"tools\": registry.names()},\n136\t        )\n137\t        messages: list[dict[str, Any]] = [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": task}]\n138\t        try:\n139\t            while True:\n140\t                budget.check_step()\n141\t                messages, compacted = _compact(messages)\n142\t                request = {\n143\t                    \"model\": self.deps.settings.model_id,\n144\t                    \"system\": self.system_prompt,\n145\t                    \"messages\": messages,\n146\t                    \"tools\": registry.schemas(),\n147\t                    \"max_tokens\": 4096,\n148\t                }\n149\t                ctx = await measure_context(self.client, request, compacted)\n150\t                response = await self.client.messages.create(**request)\n151\t                budget.charge_model(self.deps.settings.model_id, response.usage)\n152\t                await budget.flush(pool)\n153\t                ctx = ctx.finalize(response.usage)\n154\t                decision = await audit.record(\n155\t                    pool, ident, kind=\"model_decision\", parent=run_node, context=ctx,\n156\t                    payload={\n157\t                        \"requested_model\": request[\"model\"],\n158\t                        \"served_model\": response.model,\n159\t                        \"stop_reason\": response.stop_reason,\n160\t                        \"proposed_tools\": [b.name for b in response.content if b.type == \"tool_use\"],\n161\t                    },\n162\t                )\n163\t                messages.append({\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": response.content})\n164\t                uses = [b for b in response.content if b.type == \"tool_use\"]\n165\t                if not uses:\n166\t                    final = \"\".join(b.text for b in response.content if b.type == \"text\")\n167\t                    await audit.record(pool, ident, kind=\"run_finished\", parent=run_node, context=ctx,\n168\t                                       payload={\"final_sha256\": audit.digest(final)})\n169\t                    return final\n170\t                results = []\n171\t                for use in uses:\n172\t                    budget.check_tool_call()\n173\t                    results.append(await self.deps.execute_tool(ident, registry, use, decision, ctx))\n174\t                messages.append({\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": results})"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c082317-0c45-4607-a4a6-45d494611ea8","uuid":"091fedc2-e5fd-4afe-a61b-3f34c57ff7cd","timestamp":"2026-10-02T16:10:54.931Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-challenger-d0kx3atq/agent/app/loop.py","content":"    return {\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": tool_use_id, \"is_error\": True, \"content\": message}\n\n\ndef _compact(messages: list[dict]) -> tuple[list[dict], bool]:\n    if len(messages) <= COMPACT_AFTER_MESSAGES:\n        return messages, False\n    head, tail = messages[:1], messages[-KEEP_RECENT_MESSAGES:]\n    while tail and tail[0][\"role\"] != \"assistant\":\n        tail = tail[1:]\n    note = {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"[earlier tool exchanges were removed to save space]\"}\n    return head + [note] + tail, True\n\n\nclass ProcurementAgent:\n    def __init__(self, *, client, deps: AgentDeps, system_prompt: str, role: str = \"procurement\"):\n        self.client = client\n        self.deps = deps\n        self.system_prompt = system_prompt\n        self.role = role\n\n    async def run(self, ident: RunIdentity, task: str) -> str | None:\n        pool = self.deps.pool\n        await killswitch.assert_running(pool, ident.tenant)\n        budget = Budget.for_run(self.deps.settings.budgets, ident)\n        await budget.reserve_run_start(pool)\n        self.deps._budgets[ident.run_id] = budget\n        registry = build_registry(self.role, ident, self.deps)\n\n        run_node = await audit.record(\n            pool, ident, kind=\"run_started\",\n            payload={\"task_sha256\": hashlib.sha256(task.encode()).hexdigest(), \"tools\": registry.names()},\n        )\n        messages: list[dict[str, Any]] = [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": task}]\n        try:\n            while True:\n                budget.check_step()\n                messages, compacted = _compact(messages)\n                request = {\n                    \"model\": self.deps.settings.model_id,\n                    \"system\": self.system_prompt,\n                    \"messages\": messages,\n                    \"tools\": registry.schemas(),\n                    \"max_tokens\": 4096,\n                }\n                ctx = await measure_context(self.client, request, compacted)\n                response = await self.client.messages.create(**request)\n                budget.charge_model(self.deps.settings.model_id, response.usage)\n                await budget.flush(pool)\n                ctx = ctx.finalize(response.usage)\n                decision = await audit.record(\n                    pool, ident, kind=\"model_decision\", parent=run_node, context=ctx,\n                    payload={\n                        \"requested_model\": request[\"model\"],\n                        \"served_model\": response.model,\n                        \"stop_reason\": response.stop_reason,\n                        \"proposed_tools\": [b.name for b in response.content if b.type == \"tool_use\"],\n                    },\n                )\n                messages.append({\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": response.content})\n                uses = [b for b in response.content if b.type == \"tool_use\"]\n                if not uses:\n                    final = \"\".join(b.text for b in response.content if b.type == \"text\")\n                    await audit.record(pool, ident, kind=\"run_finished\", parent=run_node, context=ctx,\n                                       payload={\"final_sha256\": audit.digest(final)})\n                    return final\n                results = []\n                for use in uses:\n                    budget.check_tool_call()\n                    results.append(await self.deps.execute_tool(ident, registry, use, decision, ctx))\n                messages.append({\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": results})","numLines":70,"startLine":105,"totalLines":187}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfdhj951g4bZscWz9uHj1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Te8XWefft9iufj7UDjwuK4","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-challenger-d0kx3atq/agent/README.md","offset":20,"limit":50},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1189,"cache_read_input_tokens":13744,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1189},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c082317-0c45-4607-a4a6-45d494611ea8","uuid":"89462ca9-a45a-4a4e-9956-0f446db20afa","timestamp":"2026-10-02T16:10:56.110Z","request_id":"req_011Cfdhj8fx3mCLbwaYmzD7E","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Te8XWefft9iufj7UDjwuK4":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-challenger-d0kx3atq/agent/README.md","offset":20,"limit":50}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Te8XWefft9iufj7UDjwuK4","type":"tool_result","content":"20\t                                   |     post_slack_message -> Slack (via slack-proxy)\n21\t                                   |     memory_read, memory_write -> dept_notes\n22\t```\n23\t\n24\t* **Tenancy.** Each run belongs to one business unit, taken from the `bu`\n25\t  claim of the caller's verified OIDC token. Documents, notes, approvals and\n26\t  quotas are keyed by business unit.\n27\t* **Identity.** The agent runs as the `procurement-agent` service account.\n28\t  Its projected token (10-minute lifetime) is exchanged at the internal STS\n29\t  for audience-bound tokens for the ERP gateway, payments API and Slack\n30\t  proxy. User tokens are never forwarded.\n31\t* **Approvals.** `create_purchase_order`, `pay_invoice` and vendor messages\n32\t  require an approval from a role listed in `config/policy.yaml`. Approval\n33\t  requests are posted to `#approvals-<bu>` with the argument summary.\n34\t* **Budgets.** Per-run step, time, token, cost, tool-rate and sub-agent\n35\t  limits, plus per-user, per-business-unit and fleet quotas for daily spend\n36\t  and run starts. See `config/policy.yaml`.\n37\t* **Audit.** Every run step is a row in `audit_events` linked to its parent\n38\t  step, with the six identity fields, policy version, approval id and\n39\t  decision-time context size. The agent's database role can insert audit\n40\t  rows but not update or delete them.\n41\t\n42\t## Context size\n43\t\n44\tLogged on every audit row as `context_tokens` and `context_method`:\n45\t\n46\t| method | meaning |\n47\t|---|---|\n48\t| `count_tokens_api` | exact request counted with the provider's token-count endpoint before the call (includes cached prefix) |\n49\t| `usage_sum_estimate` | counting failed; `input_tokens + cache_read + cache_creation` from the response |\n50\t| `unavailable` | neither available; `context_tokens` is NULL, never 0 |\n51\t\n52\t`context_compacted` is true when the harness dropped earlier turns before the\n53\tcall (`app/loop.py:_compact`). Provider-side truncation is not visible.\n54\t\n55\t## Operating\n56\t\n57\t* **Halt.** Insert or update a row in `control_flags` (`scope = 'fleet'` or\n58\t  `'tenant:<bu>'`, `halted = true`) as `procurement_ops`. New runs refuse to\n59\t  start while a halt is set.\n60\t* **Release.** Merges to `main` build, sign (keyless cosign), and attest the\n61\t  image (SLSA provenance and CycloneDX SBOM). Kyverno rejects unsigned or\n62\t  unattested images in `procurement-prod`.\n63\t* **Network.** Default-deny egress with explicit rules for DNS, the egress\n64\t  proxy, the Slack proxy, the database, the ERP gateway and the STS.\n65\t\n66\t## Tests\n67\t\n68\t```bash\n69\tpip install -e '.[test]'"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c082317-0c45-4607-a4a6-45d494611ea8","uuid":"81c6b7b7-cf0f-4680-afc2-ab824230da94","timestamp":"2026-10-02T16:10:56.117Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-challenger-d0kx3atq/agent/README.md","content":"                                   |     post_slack_message -> Slack (via slack-proxy)\n                                   |     memory_read, memory_write -> dept_notes\n```\n\n* **Tenancy.** Each run belongs to one business unit, taken from the `bu`\n  claim of the caller's verified OIDC token. Documents, notes, approvals and\n  quotas are keyed by business unit.\n* **Identity.** The agent runs as the `procurement-agent` service account.\n  Its projected token (10-minute lifetime) is exchanged at the internal STS\n  for audience-bound tokens for the ERP gateway, payments API and Slack\n  proxy. User tokens are never forwarded.\n* **Approvals.** `create_purchase_order`, `pay_invoice` and vendor messages\n  require an approval from a role listed in `config/policy.yaml`. Approval\n  requests are posted to `#approvals-<bu>` with the argument summary.\n* **Budgets.** Per-run step, time, token, cost, tool-rate and sub-agent\n  limits, plus per-user, per-business-unit and fleet quotas for daily spend\n  and run starts. See `config/policy.yaml`.\n* **Audit.** Every run step is a row in `audit_events` linked to its parent\n  step, with the six identity fields, policy version, approval id and\n  decision-time context size. The agent's database role can insert audit\n  rows but not update or delete them.\n\n## Context size\n\nLogged on every audit row as `context_tokens` and `context_method`:\n\n| method | meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `count_tokens_api` | exact request counted with the provider's token-count endpoint before the call (includes cached prefix) |\n| `usage_sum_estimate` | counting failed; `input_tokens + cache_read + cache_creation` from the response |\n| `unavailable` | neither available; `context_tokens` is NULL, never 0 |\n\n`context_compacted` is true when the harness dropped earlier turns before the\ncall (`app/loop.py:_compact`). Provider-side truncation is not visible.\n\n## Operating\n\n* **Halt.** Insert or update a row in `control_flags` (`scope = 'fleet'` or\n  `'tenant:<bu>'`, `halted = true`) as `procurement_ops`. New runs refuse to\n  start while a halt is set.\n* **Release.** Merges to `main` build, sign (keyless cosign), and attest the\n  image (SLSA provenance and CycloneDX SBOM). Kyverno rejects unsigned or\n  unattested images in `procurement-prod`.\n* **Network.** Default-deny egress with explicit rules for DNS, the egress\n  proxy, the Slack proxy, the database, the ERP gateway and the STS.\n\n## Tests\n\n```bash\npip install -e '.[test]'","numLines":50,"startLine":20,"totalLines":72}}}
